Let first be "123".
Let second be "456".
Let last first be the last position of first.
Let last second be the last position of second.
Let first digits be an empty list of whole numbers.
Let second digits be an empty list of whole numbers.
For every position from 0 to last first.
Let at be last first minus position.
Let digit be character at of first minus 48.
Append digit to first digits.

For every position from 0 to last second.
Let at be last second minus position.
Let digit be character at of second minus 48.
Append digit to second digits.

Let total be last first plus last second plus 2.
Let result be a list of total zeros.
For every left from 0 to last first.
For every right from 0 to last second.
Let product be item left of first digits times item right of second digits.
Let index be left plus right.
Let sum be item index of result plus product.
Set item index of result to sum modulo 10.
Set item (index plus 1) of result to item (index plus 1) of result plus sum divided by 10.

Let result last be total minus 1.
Let output be empty text.
Let started be 0.
For every step from 0 to result last.
Let at be result last minus step.
Let digit be item at of result.
If digit is more than 0 or started is 1 or step is result last.
Append 48 plus digit to output.
Set started to 1.

Print output.
